# Node / build
node_modules/
dist/
*.log

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# LevelDB internals — locks and write-ahead logs aren't part of the pack content.
# The actual content is in *.ldb sstables + CURRENT + MANIFEST-* files.
packs/*/LOCK
packs/*/LOG
packs/*/LOG.old

# `lost/` is what LevelDB's repair pass writes when it rebuilds a manifest: the
# files it could not place, not pack content. Recovering `crows-traits` left one
# behind holding two zero-byte write-ahead logs and a stale manifest.
packs/*/lost/

# A LevelDB opened at the wrong path mints an empty database directory INSIDE
# the pack — `packs/crows-traits/crows-traits/` was tracked for exactly this
# reason. The rules above only match one level down, so pin the nested case too.
packs/*/*/

# Local-only dev tooling — not part of the public release.
dev/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
AGENTS.md

# .planning/ IS tracked as of 2026-08-20 — the Playtest 2 migration and execution
# plans are the design record for v0.2.0 and were previously untracked, i.e. one
# bad redirection from being lost. Note these become public on push.

# Internal agent scratch — plans/specs from the old workflow, not for publication.
docs/superpowers/

# docs/discrepancies/ and docs/RULES-BREAKDOWN.md ARE tracked as of 2026-08-20.
# They are errata reports and structural analysis, not rules text: ~75 words of
# quoted MCDM prose across the whole set, all of it quoted in order to argue
# about it. packs/ already ships all 437 transcribed documents publicly, so
# these add no exposure the compendiums don't already carry — and the errata are
# the feedback the playtest exists to collect.

# Note: /packs/ (built LevelDB) IS committed so the system installs and runs
# without a build step. Source YAML lives under src/packs/ for contributors.
